<title>USA: TCI Chairman Malone to relinquish presidency - WSJ.</title>
<headline>TCI Chairman Malone to relinquish presidency - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tele-Communications Inc's Chairman John Malone is expected to step aside as president as part of his strategy to turn around the company, the Wall Street Journal said Friday.</p>
<p>According to the report, people familiar with the plan believe Malone's top choice as successor is Leo Hindery Jr, the head of a San Francisco based cable operator that is partly owned by TCI.</p>
<p>The report said the TCI board could meet as early as today to consider the matter.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
